Usage: gccli goals add --period=STRING <name> [flags]

Add an activity goal.

Arguments:
  <name>    Goal name, 1 to 49 characters.

Flags:
  -h, --help                   Show context-sensitive help.
  -j, --json                   Output as JSON ($GCCLI_JSON).
      --plain                  Output as plain text (TSV) ($GCCLI_PLAIN).
      --header                 Print the column names as the first line of
                               --plain output ($GCCLI_HEADER).
      --color="auto"           Color mode: auto, always, never ($GCCLI_COLOR).
      --account=STRING         Garmin account email ($GCCLI_ACCOUNT).
      --units="auto"           Unit system for distances, speeds, paces,
                               elevations and weights in table and plain output:
                               auto (Garmin profile), metric, statute_us,
                               statute_uk ($GCCLI_UNITS).
      --version                Print version information.

      --period=STRING          Goal period: seven-days, thirty-days, one-month
                               or annual.
      --activity-type="all"    Activity type key, as activities types prints it
                               (e.g. running, cycling), or all.
      --start=DATE             First day of the goal (YYYY-MM-DD, today,
                               yesterday, 3d, +30d). Defaults to today, and to
                               the first day of this month for a one-month goal.
      --distance=DISTANCE      Distance to cover (e.g. 50km, 30mi, 5000m).
      --duration=DURATION      Time to spend (e.g. 10h, 90m).
      --calories=KCAL          Kilocalories to burn.
      --activities=N           Number of activities to do.

